# ==============================================================================
# TRIVY CONFIGURATION IGNORE FILE
# ==============================================================================
# The exceptions below address static analysis warnings that are false positives
# for raw template variables or conflict with OpenShift Container Platform runtime
# security behaviors.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KSV-0125 (AVD-KSV-0125): Restrict container images to trusted registries
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why Ignored:
# Container registry, org, and image names are parameterized in the template files
# (e.g. "${REGISTRY}/${ORG_NAME}/${NAME}/...") so they can be injected dynamically
# at deploy time. Statically parsing these template strings causes Trivy to flag
# the parameter expressions as untrusted/invalid registry URLs. The default values
# (like ghcr.io) are trusted.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KSV0125
AVD-KSV-0125

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KSV-0020 & KSV-0021 (AVD-KSV-0020 & AVD-KSV-0021): Runs with UID/GID <= 10000
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why Ignored:
# These alerts complain that the pod securityContext does not hardcode a specific
# non-root user/group ID greater than 10000 (e.g., runAsUser: 10001).
#
# On BC Gov's OpenShift Container Platform (Silver/Gold/Emerald clusters), the
# Security Context Constraints (SCC) controller dynamically allocates a safe,
# random range of extremely high UIDs/GIDs (e.g., 1000600000 to 1000609999)
# at runtime.
#
# DO NOT resolve this by hardcoding a specific UID/GID in your manifests. Doing so
# will cause the OpenShift admission controller to REJECT your pods because the
# hardcoded ID won't match the namespace's allocated dynamic range.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KSV020
KSV021
AVD-KSV-0020
AVD-KSV-0021

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KSV-0030 & KSV-0104 (AVD-KSV-0030 & AVD-KSV-0104): seccompProfile
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why Ignored:
# The standard OpenShift restricted SCC forbids setting custom seccomp profiles
# ("seccomp may not be set") as the platform configures security filters on nodes.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KSV030
KSV104
AVD-KSV-0030
AVD-KSV-0104

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KSV-0013 (AVD-KSV-0013): Image tag ':latest' used
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why Ignored:
# False positive on templated image references. The OpenShift templates use
# "${NAME}/<component>:${IMAGE_TAG}" and the pipeline always sets IMAGE_TAG
# explicitly (commit SHA for DEV previews, PR number for TEST).
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
KSV0013
KSV-0013
AVD-KSV-0013

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-3260: Reported by OSV against Undertow
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Why Ignored:
# Status verified 2026-09-06: Red Hat states that the assigning CNA marked this
# CVE Rejected. Source: https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/cve-2026-3260
#
# Keep this suppression unless a distinct, confirmed Undertow issue needs review.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CVE-2026-3260
